  "_meta": {
    "patch": "4.10",
    "updated": "2026-09-03",
    "source": "Data.p4k > Game2.dcb > libs/foundry/records/crafting/qualityquantization/quantization_<material>.xml",
    "notes": "Every material's eight quality bands, read out of the game's own DataCore rather than scraped: a terminal never shows a quality that is not one of these. Extract with `unp4k extract <Data.p4k> \"*.dcb\"` then `starbreaker dcb extract --dcb Game2.dcb -o <dir> --format xml`, and read the mappedValue of each band. A material matches a resource type by name, by \"<name> (...)\" for its ore and raw variants, and by anything in `also`. The 500 that crafting materials also carry is not from here - it is what dismantling looted spawned gear returns - so the sync adds it to every refined and gem row instead."
  },
